---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — 0x7ouda"
  description="How the research lab handles search, browser storage, external services, and privacy."
>
  <section class="container page-intro">
    <span class="eyebrow">THE SHORT VERSION</span>

    <h1>
      Your reading is <em>yours.</em>
    </h1>

    <p>
      No advertising pixels or behavioral analytics. Search runs in your
      browser.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="container prose-page article-prose">
    <h2>Reading and search</h2>

    <p>
      The website is served through GitHub Pages. Hosting providers may process
      request metadata as part of delivering and securing the site. Search
      queries are processed locally after downloading the search index; they are
      not sent to a search service.
    </p>

    <h2>Browser storage</h2>

    <p>
      A session flag may be stored in your browser to prevent the opening
      animation from repeating during the same session. This does not create an
      account or synchronize your reading activity. You can clear site data
      through your browser controls.
    </p>

    <h2>External services</h2>

    <p>
      Some links may take you to external services such as GitHub or Discord.
      Those services operate independently and are subject to their own privacy
      practices. The research lab does not receive your account credentials from
      those services.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions or privacy requests</h2>

    <p>
      Contact the lab through <a href={site.github}>the GitHub profile</a>. Do
      not post private addresses, credentials, personal information, or
      sensitive incident evidence in a public discussion.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>